// bengali-demo — Bengali–Assamese script typesetting in texish.
//
// Render with:  texish-cli scripts/bengali-demo.script
//
// The Bengali script is written left to right, so it needs none of the
// bidirectional reordering Hebrew and Arabic do. What it needs instead is work
// inside each syllable. A consonant carries an inherent vowel; a following vowel
// sign (a matra) attaches above, below, before or after it; and a consonant joined
// to the next by the hasant (the virama, U+09CD) fuses into a conjunct.
//
// The engine segments the run into orthographic syllables, then for each one asks
// the bundled Noto Serif Bengali font's GSUB table to build the conjuncts, reorders
// the pre-base i, e and ai signs — typed after their consonant but drawn before the
// whole syllable — splits the two-part o and au signs into a front part and a
// trailing part, and asks GSUB again for the width-matched vowel variants. The
// below- and above-base signs, and the reph, are then placed with the same GPOS
// anchors the engine uses for Hebrew points and Arabic dots.
//
// \font bengali selects the bundled face (also \font assamese), in a regular and a
// bold cut. No \rtl is needed — the script is left to right.

\use{document}

\title{The Bengali--Assamese Script in \TeXish}
\author{The texish engine}
\maketitle

\section{Setting a Bengali paragraph}

Each syllable is shaped on its own and the syllables are set left to right. Within a
syllable the consonants may fuse and the vowel signs attach around the base; between
syllables the line breaker finds its breaks at the interword spaces exactly as for
Latin text.

\medskip

{\font bengali 14 regular
বাংলা একটি সমৃদ্ধ ভাষা। এটি বাঁ দিক থেকে ডান দিকে লেখা হয়। প্রতিটি অক্ষর একটি ব্যঞ্জন এবং
তার সঙ্গের স্বর মিলে তৈরি হয়, আর দুটি ব্যঞ্জন হসন্ত দিয়ে যুক্ত হয়ে যুক্তাক্ষর গঠন করে।
}

\section{The pre-base vowel signs}

The i, e and ai signs are typed after their consonant but drawn before it. In each word
below the sign appears at the left of its syllable even though it follows the consonant
in memory --- day, country, and made:

\medskip

{\font bengali 16 regular
দিন   দেশ   তৈরি
}

\section{The two-part o and au signs}

The o and au signs are single characters that render in two pieces --- an e-sign before
the base and an aa-sign (for o) or a length mark (for au) after it. The engine splits
them before shaping, as in these words for horse, total, and boat:

\medskip

{\font bengali 16 regular
ঘোড়া   মোট   নৌকা
}

\section{Conjuncts}

Two consonants joined by the hasant fuse into a conjunct. The classics --- student,
knowledge, hardship, and the double-da of the word for learning:

\medskip

{\font bengali 16 regular
ছাত্র   জ্ঞান   কষ্ট   বিদ্যা
}

\section{Reph, ya-phalaa and below-base ra}

The consonant \italic{ra} takes special forms when it joins another. A word-initial ra
followed by the hasant becomes a reph --- a small stroke drawn above the following base,
though it is typed first --- as in the words for work and religion. A ya after the hasant
becomes the post-base ya-phalaa, and a ra after another consonant hangs below it, as in
love and village:

\medskip

{\font bengali 16 regular
কর্ম   ধর্ম   মধ্য   প্রেম   গ্রাম
}

\section{Nukta consonants}

A dot below a consonant --- the nukta --- forms the letters rra, rha and yya. The base
and its dot compose into a single letter, as in the everyday words for big, car and river:

\medskip

{\font bengali 16 regular
বড়   গাড়ি   নদী   আষাঢ়
}

\section{Independent vowels and signs}

A vowel that opens a syllable is written with its own independent letter, not a matra.
The below- and above-base signs stack onto their base:

\medskip

{\font bengali 16 regular
অ আ ই ঈ উ ঊ এ ঐ ও ঔ
}

\medskip

{\font bengali 16 regular
কু কূ কে কৈ কো কৌ কং কঃ
}

\section{Assamese}

The same script serves Assamese, which uses its own \italic{ro} and \italic{wo} letters. The
\verb|\font assamese| alias selects the same face:

\medskip

{\font assamese 16 regular
অসমীয়া ভাষা   ৰং   কামৰূপ
}

\section{A closing line}

A greeting, set in the bold cut:

\medskip

{\font bengali 18 bold
নমস্কার! এটি বাংলা লিপিতে লেখা হয়েছে।
}
